# Visage Bandit's copy exception, "except it's a Shapeshifter Rogue in addition to its other types", becomes part of the copy's
# copiable values (CR 707.9b), so it is in the type line of the permanent. Bot1 casts the Bandit and, holding priority, its own
# Artificial Evolution on the spell, replacing "Rogue" with "Goblin" (CR 612.1, 612.2); the effect goes on applying to the
# permanent the spell becomes (CR 400.7a). The Bandit enters as a copy of Bot1's Ornithopter and is a Goblin Shapeshifter Thopter,
# not a Rogue.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Island
Visage Bandit
Mox Sapphire
Artificial Evolution
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
